\begin{abstract}
The Astromorphic Dynamic Stability Engine Simulation Software (ADS-ESS v4.1) is a high-energy physics simulation framework integrating quantum chromodynamics (QCD) topology construction, particle-in-cell (PIC) evolution, confinement-pressure encryption, and suprakernel-grade stability validation. The system ingests multi-format QCD datasets, constructs dynamic topological substrates, evolves quark--gluon states using a QCD PIC engine, and applies quantum-resistant encryption to all state transitions. This manuscript presents the architecture, mathematical foundations, computational methodology, and stability governance underlying ADS-ESS v4.1.
\end{abstract}

\section*{Keywords}
QCD simulation; particle-in-cell; confinement pressure; suprakernel integrity; encrypted scientific computation; topological stability; quark--gluon dynamics.

