High-energy physics simulations require accurate modeling of quark--gluon interactions, confinement dynamics, and topological evolution. ADS-ESS v4.1 introduces a unified architecture combining QCD topology, PIC evolution, and confinement-pressure encryption under suprakernel authority. The system operates on RHIC/LHC telemetry, QCD lattice data, and QCDN-D matter models, producing encrypted, topology-consistent evolution logs.

